WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.804
Step 1. Open the list of immunization policies.

1.2
00:00:03.804 --> 00:00:09.400
A policy is a named list of planned vaccine doses, called recommendations.

1.3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:15.269
In the facility settings, under Clinical, select Immunization policies.

2.1
00:00:15.269 --> 00:00:19.239
Step 2. Start a new policy. Select New policy.

2.2
00:00:19.239 --> 00:00:26.047
Care opens New immunization policy, with the Facility badge next to the title.

3.1
00:00:26.047 --> 00:00:31.158
Step 3. Enter the name and the description. Policy name is required.

3.2
00:00:31.158 --> 00:00:36.592
Users choose the policy by this name when they apply it to a patient.

4.1
00:00:36.592 --> 00:00:40.611
Step 4. Choose one dose or a group of doses.

4.2
00:00:40.611 --> 00:00:44.209
A new policy starts as one recommendation.

4.3
00:00:44.209 --> 00:00:49.506
This policy has three doses, so select Type, then Group.

5.1
00:00:49.506 --> 00:00:52.186
Step 5. Add the doses to the group.

5.2
00:00:52.186 --> 00:00:56.628
Select the group in the outline, then select Add recommendation.

5.3
00:00:56.628 --> 00:01:01.848
Care adds the recommendation at the end of the group and selects it.

6.1
00:01:01.848 --> 00:01:06.801
Step 6. Set the vaccines and the timing of each recommendation.

6.2
00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:11.205
Add the vaccine code, target disease, dose and day offsets.

6.3
00:01:11.205 --> 00:01:34.458
Duplicate copies a dose with its values; then change the dose and timing.

7.1
00:01:34.458 --> 00:01:41.030
Step 7. Save the policy. Select Save policy. Care shows Immunization policy created,

7.2
00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:47.249
and the new policy is at the top of the list with its three recommendations.
